<% content_for :summary do %>
  Moderation flagged a reply by <%= @reply.member.name %> and hid it.
<% end %>

<p>
  <a href="<%= member_url(@reply.member, host: @community.host) %>">
    <%= @reply.member.name %></a> (<em><%= @reply.member.email %></em>) posted
  <a href="<%= post_reply_url(@post, @reply, host: @community.host) %>">
    a reply</a> in
  <a href="<%= posts_url(host: @community.host) %>">
    <%= @community.name %></a>, and OpenAI Moderation flagged it as disallowed.
</p>
<p>
  The reply has been hidden and is not visible to other members. It is excluded from email notifications, including the newsletter, while hidden.
</p>
<p>
  Flagged <%= "category".pluralize(@moderation_score.flagged_categories.count) %>: <em><%= @moderation_score.flagged_categories.join(', ') %></em>
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Action required:</strong> Review the reply, and either delete it or un-hide it
</p>

<% if @community.open_ai_member_moderation_enabled %>
<p>
  Based on your
    <a href="<%= settings_moderation_url(host: @community.host) %>">
      moderation settings</a>, the <strong>member's account has been deactivated</strong>.
  They cannot log in and are currently not receiving email notifications.
  <strong>Reactivate the account</strong> on
  <a href="<%= member_url(@post.member, host: @community.host) %>">
  their profile</a>.
<p>
<% else %>
<p>
  Based on your
  <a href="<%= settings_moderation_url(host: @community.host) %>">
    moderation settings</a>, the member's account is still active.
</p>
<% end %>

<% content_for :button_label do %>
  View reply &rarr;
<% end %>

<% content_for :button_link do %><%= post_reply_url(@post, @reply, host: @community.host) %><% end %>
